-- §1  The remainder and its fit, read off the ranges rather than off a point.
# One row per layer that files both a demand range and a nameplate range and classifies itself,
# carrying both ranges and the sign the document filed, so the example can recompute `r = n - d`
# in Rust and assert the two agree.
#
# The interesting column is `sign!`
#   Run it alone and look there: a `transition` is the case a two-member enumeration could not
#   have named, and the corpus almost never reaches it.
#
# `evidence!` separates the corpus from the fixtures
#   The split is the point. Every fixture layer reaching this query is a `transition`: they were
#   written to exercise the state the corpus almost never reaches, so a census pooling them would
#   report the rare case as common and the note would quote it.
#
# The shared relation is layers/signed.sqlc
#   It is also what the sign rule examines. The example and the checker therefore range over the
#   same rows by construction rather than by two authors agreeing.
#
# The pin this query owes: `differenceable!`
#   `differenceable!` is the pin this query owes its caller. Without it the example accuses a
#   correct filing. `r = n - d` read off the two filed totals is the remainder only where those
#   totals were not both scaled by one conversion factor with width. Where they were, differencing
#   counts that factor's spread twice and the range says `transition` about a layer that clears.
#   composition/unsettled.sqlc names exactly those layers; composition/fused_remainders.sqlc carries
#   their actual remainder.
-- layers/signed.sqlc, with the evidence axis from pm.filing.
SELECT s.filing              AS "filing!",
       s.layer               AS "layer!",
       s.d_low::float8       AS "d_low!",
       s.d_mode::float8      AS "d_mode!",
       s.d_high::float8      AS "d_high!",
       s.n_low::float8       AS "n_low!",
       s.n_mode::float8      AS "n_mode!",
       s.n_high::float8      AS "n_high!",
       s.sign::text          AS "sign!",
       f.evidence            AS "evidence!",
       (u.filing IS NULL)    AS "differenceable!"
FROM (
    :compose(layers/signed.sqlc)
) s
JOIN (
    :compose(scope/every_filing.sqlc)
) f USING (filing)
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(composition/unsettled.sqlc)
) u ON u.filing = s.filing AND u.layer = s.layer
ORDER BY s.filing, s.layer
